{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-51b3f748-5d84-4ff6-8ec5-59357106ca37","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95abf611fd28adeb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-xz7q2_e8/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigate plugin workspace-resolution initialization dependencies\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether workspace resolution in the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package (the `kubernetes-auth` auth plugin and the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) can initialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mappings in a server context where the tracking store and model registry store are not initialized. The strategy flags this as an open question with two bounded outcomes, and the answer determines the scope of both the plugin extension work and the MLflow server's workspace-provider-only initialization path for artifacts-only serving.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the initialization path of the workspace store / workspace provider in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins`: what it constructs, what it reads, and whether any step requires a tracking store, model registry store, or full tracking-server initialization to have happened first.\n- Trace how artifact request paths under the S3 artifact store structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) can be resolved to a parent experiment and then to its workspace assignment without consulting a tracking store; identify any lookup that currently routes through initialized stores.\n- Document the two bounded outcomes:\n  - **Outcome A — not coupled**: workspace resolution runs in the artifacts-only context as-is; the downstream work is verification and test coverage only.\n  - **Outcome B — coupled**: workspace resolution depends on tracking-store-backed initialization; document exactly wha