ly based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Operator validation of the split-topology configuration: reject configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation), and keep a single MLflow CR as the declarative configuration surface so users do not manage individual resources.\n- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n- Deployments that do not enable the split topology are unaffected — the dedicated instance and routing are created only for CRs that opt in.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, its container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing mechanism — measured by artifact requests against the main tracking entry point being served by the dedicated instance.\n- The operator rejects (with a clear status condition or error) a split-topology configuration in which the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags.\n- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when the Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime, matching the operator's existing conditional-dependency behavior.\n- Deployments whose MLflow CRs do not enable the split topology reconcile identically to before — measured by the operator's existing test suite passing.\n- The deployed split topology passes the end-to-end workspace-validated artifact serving scenarios (member served HTTP 200, non-member denied HTTP 403, workspace store unreachable denied fail-closed) against the operator-deployed instances, using a server image that supports the combined flags.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\"\n- P1: \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\"\n- Supports the strategy's split-server topology direction from the Staff Engineer / SME Input (split deployment, not a configuration toggle).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":62158,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c411d79be451aa1","agent_id":"aca432ed42d3c5a72","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"78ec4377-5238-4f73-b0ca-a61c0188cdeb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:10:50.327Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
