{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81b0479c8befd4fb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for artifacts-only serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing investigation selects tracking-server delegation\n15\t    instead of gateway-level routing, the HTTPRoute design changes and configuration\n16\t    support for delegating artifact operations is added to the main tracking deployment;\n17\t    the dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and workspace flag propagation\n18\t    are unaffected.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for artifacts-only serving\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, forming a split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the dedicated artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator also configures the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, using the routing mechanism selected by the routing investigation.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- New Helm chart templates (rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern: MLflow CR spec → Helm values → embedded chart templates → Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, its Service, and its HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n45\t- Workspace configuration propagation to the artifacts-only instance (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment; the artifacts-only Deployment runs with the combined flag set including `--artifacts-only` and `--serve-artifacts`.\n46\t- Artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated instance, implemented per the routing mechanism selected by the routing investigation (gateway-level path routing via HTTPRoute, or tracking-server delegation configuration if that is the selected outcome).\n47\t- Gateway API HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n48\t- Operator validation of the split-topology configuration: reject configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation), and keep a single MLflow CR as the declarative configuration surface so users do not manage individual resources.\n49\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n50\t- Deployments that do not enable the split topology are unaffected — the dedicated instance and routing are created only for CRs that opt in.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n55\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, its container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n56\t- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing mechanism — measured by artifact requests against the main tracking entry point being served by the dedicated instance.\n57\t- The operator rejects (with a clear status condition or error) a split-topology configuration in which the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags.\n58\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when the Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime, matching the operator's existing conditional-dependency behavior.\n59\t- Deployments whose MLflow CRs do not enable the split topology reconcile identically to before — measured by the operator's existing test suite passing.\n60\t- The deployed split topology passes the end-to-end workspace-validated artifact serving scenarios (member served HTTP 200, non-member denied HTTP 403, workspace store unreachable denied fail-closed) against the operator-deployed instances, using a server image that supports the combined flags.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- P1: \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\"\n65\t- P1: \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\"\n66\t- Supports the strategy's split-server topology direction from the Staff Engineer / SME Input (split deployment, not a configuration toggle).\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-967c1361e6a1dddf","agent_id":"a555a49846113b425","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d6