{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af278c462aee81e6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds workspace resolution is not coupled\n15\t    to tracking store initialization, this epic's scope shrinks to verification and\n16\t    test coverage in the artifacts-only context; if coupled, the scope grows to factoring\n17\t    workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tVerify and, where needed, extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the `kubernetes://` workspace store) functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The scope of this work — verification only versus refactoring — is fixed by the outcome of the investigation into the plugin's initialization dependencies.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- If the investigation determined workspace resolution is not coupled to tracking store initialization: verify the resolution path in the artifacts-only context and add test coverage exercising experiment-to-workspace resolution (including resolution from artifact request paths under the S3 structure `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) without any initialized tracking or model registry store.\n44\t- If the investigation determined workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the existing workspace-provider registration surface (`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading) so the tracking server and the artifacts-only server consume the same capability.\n45\t- Workspace authorization for artifact requests reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure; the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged, and authentication at the ingress level works identically for both server types. Kubernetes API mechanics of the authorization check are implementation details of this package, not prescribed by the strategy.\n46\t- Preserve the tracking server's existing (non-artifact) workspace resolution behavior — no regressions in workspace-scoped authorization for tracking, model registry, or prompt registry operations (all explicitly out of scope for change).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Workspace resolution resolves an experiment to its workspace assignment via the `kubernetes://` workspace store in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized — measured by a test exercising the plugin's resolution path in that context.\n51\t- Artifact request paths following the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure can be resolved to their parent experiment's workspace assignment without consulting a tracking store.\n52\t- If refactoring was required: workspace resolution initializes through an independent path, and the tracking server's existing workspace resolution behavior is unchanged — measured by the plugin's and server's existing test suites passing.\n53\t- The workspace-provider registration surface (entry point group, registry loading) is preserved, so both the tracking server and the artifacts-only server load the same provider without plugin-specific branching by the callers.\n54\t- No change is required to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar or `--app-name kubernetes-auth` configuration on either server deployment.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- P1: \"Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\"\n59\t- Supports (does not own) the P0 HLR \"Artifact requests … are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" — the server-side validation delegates to this capability.\n60\t- Addresses the strategy dependency \"mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin (internal, exists): may require extension if workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path\".\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-860f5d5e1e4d853d","agent_id":"afbd8680b7250ff64","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"0d0a807d-56b1-48c7-99e5-ddb2851eed6b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:17:56.547Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af278c462aee81e6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
