 dedicated instance's HTTPRoute design (host/path structure, relationship to the main tracking route), one of this epic's three template deliverables. True gate, action `rewrite`. Bounded outcomes (2): (A) gateway-level routing — the dedicated instance's HTTPRoute path-shares the main tracking host; (B) tracking-server delegation — the dedicated instance gets its own host/route. Scope/approach changes, not epic existence → `rewrite` gate, no branch files. |\n| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The routing mechanism (gateway-level path routing vs. tracking-server delegation) determines whether this epic is an operator-managed HTTPRoute configuration or delegation configuration on the main tracking Deployment (with server-side support coordinated with the server workstream). True gate, action `rewrite`. Same two bounded outcomes; scope/approach changes, not epic existence → `rewrite` gate, no branch files. |\n| E003 ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rules 13/14/15 | Separate codebases. The server consumes the plugin's existing workspace-provider interface (entry point group / WorkspaceStoreRegistry) — including artifact-path-to-workspace resolution, solely owned by the plugin epic per the strategy's dependency note — which E004 preserves in both outcomes; E004 does not produce a new build-against artifact. Integration is enforced by acceptance criteria on E003 (end-to-end 403/200 behavior requires the plugin capability), not a DAG edge. |\n| E005 ∥ E006 (no edge) | Rule 13 exception, Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (new artifacts-only chart templates vs. routing configuration on the main tracking side) → parallel per Rule 15. The routing configuration references the dedicated instance's Service — a configuration reference, not a build-against artifact — so the coupling is enforced by AC gates on E006 (routed-path scenarios validated against an operator-deployed dedicated instance), never a DAG edge. |\n| E005/E006 ∥ E003/E004 (no edge) | Rule 13 exception, Rule 14 | The operator's Helm templates, flags, and routing configuration are configuration references to the server's capability (flags on a container command), not a build-against artifact — the same class as an image digest. Enforced by AC gates on E005/E006 (deployed topology passes workspace-validated serving scenarios using a server image that supports the combined flags), never by a DAG edge (mirrors Rule 10's reasoning). Different repo, no shared artifacts. |"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67827,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-860f5d5e1e4d853d","agent_id":"afbd8680b7250ff64","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"151d76e0-46a4-44b5-9289-7ba1a1c002b3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:24:31.696Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
