{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85a7fdecb189bda9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate plugin workspace-resolution initialization dependencies\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate plugin workspace-resolution initialization dependencies\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve whether workspace resolution in the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` package (the `kubernetes-auth` auth plugin and the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) can initialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mappings in a server context where the tracking store and model registry store are not initialized. The strategy flags this as an open question with two bounded outcomes, and the answer determines the scope of both the plugin extension work and the MLflow server's workspace-provider-only initialization path for artifacts-only serving.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Trace the initialization path of the workspace store / workspace provider in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins`: what it constructs, what it reads, and whether any step requires a tracking store, model registry store, or full tracking-server initialization to have happened first.\n34\t- Trace how artifact request paths under the S3 artifact store structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) can be resolved to a parent experiment and then to its workspace assignment without consulting a tracking store; identify any lookup that currently routes through initialized stores.\n35\t- Document the two bounded outcomes:\n36\t  - **Outcome A — not coupled**: workspace resolution runs in the artifacts-only context as-is; the downstream work is verification and test coverage only.\n37\t  - **Outcome B — coupled**: workspace resolution depends on tracking-store-backed initialization; document exactly what must be factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin, and the impact on the tracking server's existing (non-artifact) usage of the same resolution logic.\n38\t- Produce a written determination with evidence (code paths, initialization sequence, any store-dependent lookups) and a recommended scope for the downstream plugin and server work.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- A determination document states, with code-level evidence, whether workspace store initialization and experiment-to-workspace resolution in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` depend on tracking store or model registry store availability.\n43\t- If coupled, the document enumerates the specific coupling points and the refactoring scope required to make workspace resolution independently initializable, including the effect on the tracking server's existing workspace resolution path.\n44\t- If not coupled, the document includes verification evidence (e.g., a reproducible exercise of the resolution path in an artifacts-only-style context) demonstrating the resolution works without store initialization.\n45\t- The recommendation explicitly selects one of the two bounded outcomes so the downstream plugin and server implementation scope can be finalized without further analysis.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- Enables the P0 HLRs \"Artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" and \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed\" by fixing the initialization approach the server can rely on.\n50\t- Enables the P1 HLR \"Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\" by determining whether that HLR requires verification only or refactoring.\n51\t- Resolves the strategy's Open Question 3, Assumption 2, and the risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" (whose mitigation calls for validating the plugin's initialization dependencies early).\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-952f1b81690916df","agent_id":"a6112ae6c5a7eb8d3","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"07fb188b-04c8-4102-ba2c-880b3dce3d3a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:25:26.565Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85a7fdecb189bda9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
