{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b549594920cd4b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermine how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy flags this as an open question because the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the main tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations — i.e., whether the routing can be handled entirely at the gateway level or requires server-side delegation support.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate gateway-level routing: an HTTPRoute that routes artifact API paths (e.g., the artifact-serving endpoints) from the main tracking server's host to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, with no change to the tracking server itself. Assess feasibility against the existing conditional Gateway API HTTPRoute pattern in the operator (runtime CRD discovery).\n34\t- Evaluate tracking-server delegation: a configuration change on the main tracking deployment that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated instance, including what server-side support (if any) the tracking server would need and how the operator would propagate that configuration.\n35\t- Compare the two mechanisms against the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (CR spec → Helm values → rendered templates → Server-Side Apply) and document which artifacts each option requires (HTTPRoute templates, Deployment configuration, server settings).\n36\t- Produce a recommended mechanism with a decision record covering the trade-offs (routing precision, operational surface, backwards compatibility for deployments that do not enable the split topology, and misconfiguration risk where artifact requests could bypass workspace validation).\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A decision record recommends one routing mechanism (gateway-level path routing vs. tracking-server delegation) with documented trade-offs and evidence from the operator's existing routing and Helm rendering patterns.\n41\t- The record states explicitly whether the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, so the server workstream knows whether delegation support is in its scope.\n42\t- The record specifies the HTTPRoute design implications for the dedicated artifacts-only instance (host/path structure, relationship to the main tracking route) consistent with the operator's conditional Gateway API dependency.\n43\t- The recommendation addresses the misconfiguration risk called out in the strategy (artifact requests bypassing workspace validation) and how the chosen mechanism prevents or detects it.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- Enables the P1 HLRs \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\" and \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" by fixing the routing design those deliverables implement.\n48\t- Resolves the strategy's Open Question 2 (owner: MLflow Team).\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-952f1b81690916df","agent_id":"a6112ae6c5a7eb8d3","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"65ca97ed-79ad-450a-81ab-25362e8637f4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:25:27.207Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b549594920cd4b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
