{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b589732712d618e2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing investigation selects tracking-server delegation\n15\t    instead of gateway-level routing, the dedicated instance's HTTPRoute design changes\n16\t    (dedicated host vs. path-sharing with the main tracking route); the dedicated\n17\t    Deployment, Service, and workspace flag propagation are unaffected.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MLflow operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, forming the deployment half of a split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the dedicated artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The operator propagates workspace configuration to the dedicated instance using the same mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking deployment. Configuring the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to this dedicated instance is a separable deliverable tracked as its own epic; this epic delivers the dedicated instance itself.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates (rendered through the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern: MLflow CR spec → Helm values → embedded chart templates → Server-Side Apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, its Service, and its HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n44\t- Workspace configuration propagation to the artifacts-only instance (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main tracking deployment; the artifacts-only Deployment runs with the combined flag set including `--artifacts-only` and `--serve-artifacts`.\n45\t- Gateway API HTTPRoute resources for the dedicated instance created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies; the HTTPRoute design (host/path structure, relationship to the main tracking route) follows the routing-mechanism decision record produced by the routing investigation.\n46\t- Operator validation of the split-topology configuration: reject configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation), and keep a single MLflow CR as the declarative configuration surface so users do not manage individual resources.\n47\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n48\t- Split-topology validation: the operator-deployed dedicated instance serves workspace-validated artifacts through its own entry point, using a server image that supports the combined flags.\n49\t- Deployments that do not enable the split topology are unaffected — the dedicated instance is created only for CRs that opt in.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n54\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, its container command runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n55\t- The operator rejects (with a clear status condition or error) a split-topology configuration in which the artifacts-only instance lacks the workspace flags.\n56\t- HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance are created only when the Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime, matching the operator's existing conditional-dependency behavior.\n57\t- Deployments whose MLflow CRs do not enable the split topology reconcile identically to before — measured by the operator's existing test suite passing.\n58\t- The operator-deployed dedicated artifacts-only instance passes the workspace-validated artifact serving scenarios (member served HTTP 200, non-member denied HTTP 403, workspace store unreachable denied fail-closed) against the dedicated instance's own entry point, using a server image that supports the combined flags.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- P1: \"MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute\"\n63\t- Supports the strategy's split-server topology direction from the Staff Engineer / SME Input (split deployment, not a configuration toggle).\n64\t- Delivers the deployment surface that the P1 HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" targets; that routing deliverable is tracked as a separate epic.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-952f1b81690916df","agent_id":"a6112ae6c5a7eb8d3","session_id":"115c743c-228e-470f-acfa-50e91d621e74","uuid":"bd93561d-e7bb-4ad2-a041-433fc112e97d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:25:34.703Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b589732712d618e2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
